						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "ANGLE CONVERTER\nThe Angle Converter node converts between normalized values (between 0 and 1), radians and degrees.\nIn the inspector you can switch these three for both the inlet and outlet.\n\nTransforming a normalized period value to radians can be useful when working with a cartesian plane for rotations as seen in the top part of the example.\nIn the bottom part of the example we use the Angle Converter node to convert degrees (0-360) to a period (0-1) that works with the rotation input of the Transform node."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 191.605499267578125,
